# Agent Trust Firewall needs no secrets to run.
#
# The two threat-intelligence providers the product relies on — GreyNoise
# Community and Shodan InternetDB — are keyless. The keys below are optional:
# supplying one activates an extra provider, and leaving it unset makes that
# provider report "not configured" in the UI rather than failing anything.
#
# Every one of these is read server-side only. Never prefix any of them with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ — that would inline the key into the client bundle.

# Free tier, https://www.abuseipdb.com/api — IP abuse-confidence score.
# ABUSEIPDB_API_KEY=

# Free tier, https://otx.alienvault.com/api — community threat pulses.
# OTX_API_KEY=

# Pins the gateway's X25519 keypair across restarts (64 hex chars).
# Generated at boot when unset, which is fine for a single instance.
# ATF_GATEWAY_SECRET_KEY=
